---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { ISSUES_URL, OPEN_METEO_URL, PRODUCT_NAME } from "../brand";
---

<Page
  artTop="band-horse"
  sceneBottom="reef"
  title={`Privacy: ${PRODUCT_NAME} keeps everything on your PC`}
  description={`${PRODUCT_NAME} is local-first: no account, no telemetry. The only network calls are the weather forecast and, if you give them a token, the developer tiles.`}
  label="Privacy"
  heading="Local first. Nothing phones home."
>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    {PRODUCT_NAME} has no account and no telemetry. This page lists the only two things that ever leave your PC, and what this website does.
  </Fragment>

  <section class="block reveal" aria-labelledby="pv-out">
    <h2 class="block__title" id="pv-out">What leaves your PC</h2>
    <div class="block__content table-wrap">
      <table class="table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Call</th><th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">What is sent</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><a href={OPEN_METEO_URL} rel="noopener">Open-Meteo</a> forecast and place search</th>
            <td>Only if you add a weather widget, and only after you pick a place.</td>
            <td>The place you searched for, then its coordinates. You can search by name instead of sharing your location.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Developer tiles (GitHub, Linear, Vercel)</th>
            <td>Only for a tile you add to the dock and give a token. The token is kept in Windows Credential Manager.</td>
            <td>Your token, to that service&rsquo;s own API, to read the counts the tile shows. Nothing goes to {PRODUCT_NAME}.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Nothing else. No analytics, no crash upload, no advertising identifiers.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block reveal" aria-labelledby="pv-local">
    <h2 class="block__title" id="pv-local">What stays on your PC</h2>
    <div class="block__content">
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Your layout, themes, imported wallpapers and settings, in your user profile.</li>
        <li>A snapshot of your original wallpaper and desktop settings, kept so that switching back can restore them.</li>
        <li>The last weather and system readings, cached so widgets can appear instantly.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If something goes wrong, <strong>Copy diagnostics</strong> builds a plain text bundle on your PC. It goes nowhere
        unless you paste it into an <a href={ISSUES_URL} rel="noopener">issue</a> yourself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block reveal" aria-labelledby="pv-site">
    <h2 class="block__title" id="pv-site">This website</h2>
    <div class="block__content">
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>No cookies, no analytics, no tracking pixels, no third-party scripts, fonts or CDNs. Everything is served from this site, which Vercel hosts, so as with any web request its servers see your IP address while the page loads.</li>
        <li>Your theme choice is kept in your browser&rsquo;s local storage and never sent anywhere.</li>
        <li>
          An anonymous visit counter in the footer. A browser that has not been counted today asks the site to add one to a single
          total, and every page view reads that total. The total is one number stored with Upstash Redis through Vercel. It is
          not tied to you: no IP address, cookie, account or identifier is stored, and the only thing kept in your browser is the
          date you were last counted (local storage). If the counter is unavailable, it is hidden rather than guessed.
        </li>
        <li>The live widgets on the home page read your clock and, if your browser offers it, your battery level. That happens in the page on your device; nothing is sent.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block reveal" aria-labelledby="pv-dev">
    <h2 class="block__title" id="pv-dev">Not part of the product</h2>
    <div class="block__content">
      <p>
        Development time tracking (Hackatime) was used while building the project. It is a developer tool, not a part of
        {PRODUCT_NAME}: the app does not include it or contact it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
